From: Mixtile <support@mixtile.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] usb: power_delivery: fusb302: keep the transceiver powered on handoff

Powering the transceiver down while a contract is live leaves the chip unable
to answer the source's GoodCRC, and a source that sends anything reads the
silence as a dead link and drops VBUS.

Skip the power-down while attached and PD-capable.

diff --git a/drivers/power/power_delivery/fusb302.c b/drivers/power/power_delivery/fusb302.c
index 6eaad0c..3d9c32a 100644
--- a/drivers/power/power_delivery/fusb302.c
+++ b/drivers/power/power_delivery/fusb302.c
@@ -958,12 +958,14 @@ static int fusb302_enter_low_power_mode(struct tcpc_dev *dev,
 	int ret = 0;
 	unsigned int reg;
 
+	/* PWR_MEDIUM clears TX; stay powered while a contract is live. */
+	if (attached && pd_capable)
+		return 0;
+
 	ret = fusb302_mask_interrupt(chip);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
-	if (attached && pd_capable)
-		reg = FUSB_REG_POWER_PWR_MEDIUM;
-	else if (attached)
+	if (attached)
 		reg = FUSB_REG_POWER_PWR_LOW;
 	else
 		reg = 0;
